\section{Choosing a function}{

Use \code{\link[=fit_lrd]{fit_lrd()}} for an unaugmented, unpenalized contrast model, or
\code{\link[=fit_alrd]{fit_alrd()}} for main-effect augmentation with optional lasso selection.
\code{\link[=predict_ite]{predict_ite()}} evaluates the full treated-minus-control contrast rather
than the fitted treatment contribution. Pass known design probabilities
explicitly in randomized studies. For baseline observational treatment,
use \code{\link[=estimate_ps]{estimate_ps()}} on one row per subject and map scores to visits.
}

